<%- include('partials/head') %>
<h1>Frequently Asked Questions</h1>

<div class="faq">
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What is CSBFP?</summary>
    <p>Certified Small Business Finance Professional (CSBFP) is a professional certification for individuals working in small business finance. It confirms completion of industry training, a passing assessment, and agreement to professional standards.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Who can get certified?</summary>
    <p>Individuals 18 or older who work in, or are entering, the small business finance industry. This includes brokers, funders, lenders, underwriters, operations and servicing staff, compliance and risk professionals, and managers. You do not need a current employer to apply.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What are the steps?</summary>
    <p>Create an account, complete your application and training modules, pass the assessment, and pay the annual fee. You'll then receive an invitation to complete a one-time background check. Allow 1–3 days for results. Your certification number will be issued upon approval.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What information do I need?</summary>
    <p>Your legal name, date of birth, ZIP code, email and mobile number, when you entered the industry, your current employer and role (if you have one), and the financing products you work with.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What does the training involve?</summary>
    <p>Four short modules (Industry Fundamentals, Products &amp; Terminology, Federal &amp; State Regulation, and Professional Conduct) followed by a 20-question multiple-choice assessment. You need 80% (16 of 20) to pass, and you can save your progress and come back. You have up to 10 attempts, with a 60-minute wait between them.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Is there a background check?</summary>
    <p>The program includes a one-time background screening at initial certification, focused on financial crimes and fraud. It is not repeated at renewal. <% if (!screeningEnabled) { %>Screening is not active yet. Until it is, no certification is represented as screened.<% } %> We never ask for your Social Security number on this website.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>How much does it cost?</summary>
    <p><%= program.annualFee %> a year, paid by card after you pass the assessment.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Can I get a refund?</summary>
    <p>No. Fees are non-refundable once you sign up to get certified, except where a refund is required by law.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Does it renew automatically?</summary>
    <p>Yes, every 12 months at <%= program.annualFee %>. We email you 30 days before each renewal, and you can cancel online at any time. Renewal does not repeat the background screening or the assessment.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>What if I change jobs?</summary>
    <p>Your certification belongs to you, not your employer, and your number stays the same for your whole career. Update your employer from your account at any time.</p>
  </details>
  <details name="faq">
    <summary>Can a certification be suspended or revoked?</summary>
    <p>Yes. Under the program rules, a certification can be suspended or revoked, for example for material misrepresentation or misconduct. You will be notified and can respond. Public verification shows only the status, never the reason.</p>
  </details>
</div>

<div class="actions">
  <a class="button" href="/portal/signup">Get Certified</a>
  <a class="button secondary" href="/support">Ask a Question</a>
</div>
<%- include('partials/foot') %>
